s, and the privacy manifest it ships, so you can fill in your app’s own manifest and privacy labels.","type":"text"}],"role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/privacymanifests","kind":"article"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/TrackingPlanWorkflow":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Tell the people and services that read your events what each event holds, and hear about a change that would break their data before it ships."}],"url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/trackingplanworkflow","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/TrackingPlanWorkflow","title":"Exporting and Checking a Tracking Plan","role":"article","type":"topic","kind":"article"},"doc://TrackingPlanTesting/documentation/TrackingPlanTesting":{"kind":"symbol","title":"TrackingPlanTesting","role":"collection","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Fail a Swift Testing test when an app’s events no longer match its committed tracking plan, so every change to an event comes with a change to the plan."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/TrackingPlanTesting\/documentation\/TrackingPlanTesting","url":"\/documentation\/trackingplantesting"},"doc://AppKitTracking/documentation/AppKitTracking":{"kind":"symbol","title":"AppKitTracking","role":"collection","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"Let AppKit views find their tracker up the responder chain, and track what controls do.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/appkittracking","identifier":"doc:\/\/AppKitTracking\/documentation\/AppKitTracking"},"doc://HTTPDestinations/documentation/HTTPDestinations":{"type":"topic","title":"HTTPDestinations","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Send each batch of records to an HTTP endpoint, and send it again until it arrives."}],"role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/httpdestinations","kind":"symbol"},"doc://PostHogEncoding/documentation/PostHogEncoding":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Write batches of r